---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import GuideFigure from '../../components/GuideFigure.astro';

const ethan = await getEntry('templates', 'ethan-walker');
const softic = await getEntry('templates', 'softic-studio');
if (!ethan || !softic) throw new Error('The portfolio roundup needs ethan-walker and softic-studio.');

const title = 'Best free Framer portfolio templates';
const description = 'Ten free Framer portfolio templates for designers, photographers and studios, with who each one suits and how to pick the right one.';
const url = new URL('/guides/free-framer-portfolio-templates/', Astro.site).href;

// Templates by other creators, all free on Framer Marketplace when this was written. The focus
// line is what the creator states on the listing; check the live demo before you choose.
const others = [
  { name: 'Jett', by: 'Mickael Zimmer', slug: 'jett', focus: 'A full portfolio site with a premium feel.', fit: 'Designers who want a polished, multi-page portfolio.' },
  { name: 'Tabfolio', by: 'Sebastian', slug: 'tabfolio', focus: 'A portfolio for UX and product designers.', fit: 'UX designers who show case studies more than images.' },
  { name: 'Margot', by: 'FTC Studio', slug: 'margot', focus: 'A minimal portfolio.', fit: 'Anyone who wants the work to do the talking.' },
  { name: 'Maelle', by: 'Thaer Swailem', slug: 'maelle', focus: 'A minimal portfolio listed under photography.', fit: 'Photographers and visual artists.' },
  { name: 'Kai Marlow', by: 'Lazar Filipović', slug: 'kai-marlow', focus: 'A free portfolio listed under photography.', fit: 'Photographers who want large images first.' },
  { name: 'Leo Marlowe', by: 'EV Studio', slug: 'leo-marlowe', focus: 'A portfolio for design engineers.', fit: 'Designers who also build, and want to show both.' },
  { name: 'Nuria', by: 'Nostromo Studio', slug: 'nuria', focus: 'A playful portfolio for creatives.', fit: 'Illustrators and creatives with a lighter tone.' },
  { name: 'Taylor', by: 'Akin & Ed', slug: 'taylor', focus: 'An agency and portfolio template.', fit: 'Freelancers who present themselves like a small studio.' },
];
const total = 2 + others.length;
---

<LegalPage accent="free"
  kicker="Guide"
  title={title}
  seoTitle={`${total} best free Framer portfolio templates (2026)`}
  description={description}
  updated="November 3, 2026"
  jsonLd={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: title,
    description,
    url,
    mainEntityOfPage: url,
    dateModified: '2026-11-03',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Vonex Design', url: new URL('/', Astro.site).href },
  }}
>
  <p>
    A free Framer template is the fastest way to a good portfolio: the layout, type and animation are done, and you
    only add your work. Here are {total} free portfolio templates on Framer Marketplace, who each one suits, and what
    to check before you choose.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two of them are ours, so we say so. The rest are by other Framer creators. Everything listed was free on Framer
    Marketplace on November 3, 2026.
  </p>

  <h2>How we picked</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Free to copy from Framer Marketplace.</li>
    <li>Built for a personal or studio portfolio, not a general business site.</li>
    <li>A mix of styles: minimal, bold, photo-led and case-study-led.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>1. {ethan.data.name} (ours)</h2>
  <GuideFigure template={ethan} caption={`${ethan.data.name}: ${ethan.data.tagline}`} />
  <p>
    Large type and plenty of space for a designer's portfolio. Projects and services live in the Framer CMS, so
    adding a case study does not mean editing the layout. Pages: Home, About, Work, a page per project, Contact and
    Privacy Policy.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> UI, UX and graphic designers who add projects often.</p>
  <p><a href={`/templates/${ethan.id}/`}>See {ethan.data.name}</a> · <a href="/guides/framer-portfolio-template/">Set it up step by step</a></p>

  <h2>2. {softic.data.name} (ours)</h2>
  <GuideFigure template={softic} caption={`${softic.data.name}: ${softic.data.tagline}`} />
  <p>
    A dark, bold portfolio for a design studio, with case studies in the CMS and a team section. It presents a small
    team or a freelancer as a studio.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> small agencies and freelancers who sell services, not only show work.</p>
  <p><a href={`/templates/${softic.id}/`}>See {softic.data.name}</a></p>

  {
    others.map((t, i) => (
      <Fragment>
        <h2>{i + 3}. {t.name}</h2>
        <p>{t.focus} By {t.by}.</p>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> {t.fit}</p>
        <p>
          <a href={`https://www.framer.com/marketplace/templates/${t.slug}/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            {t.name} on Framer Marketplace
          </a>
        </p>
      </Fragment>
    ))
  }

  <h2>How to choose</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Start from your work.</strong> Image-heavy work suits photo-led layouts. Case studies need long project pages.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the CMS.</strong> If you add projects often, pick a template with a projects collection.</li>
    <li><strong>Open the live demo on your phone.</strong> Most visits to a portfolio come from a phone.</li>
    <li><strong>Count the pages you need.</strong> A one-page site is fine to start; you can add pages later.</li>
    <li><strong>Read the license.</strong> Each author sets their own; ours is one <a href="/license/">template license</a> for every Vonex template.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Is a free template really free?</h2>
  <p>
    Copying the template costs nothing, and you can build and test on a free Framer account. Your own domain needs a
    paid Framer site plan. The details are in <a href="/guides/framer-pricing/">Framer pricing explained</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-xl flex flex-wrap gap-sm">
    <Button href="/templates/free/" arrow>All our free templates</Button>
    <Button href="/guides/" variant="secondary" arrow>More guides</Button>
  </div>
</LegalPage>
